course: dictionary
lesson: 3547
title: Four meanings of feel
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word feel has four jobs. It can mean to notice something with your body, to have an emotion, to seem a certain way, or to think or believe. The words around it show you which job it is doing.
explain: «Feel how soft this is» means touch it and notice. «I feel sad» means you have a feeling inside. «The water feels cold» means cold is how the water seems when you touch it.
explain: «I feel that we should help» means think or believe. To check, swap in think and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Feel is a verb (feel, feels, felt, feeling), and a feel is a noun meaning the way something feels.
fact: Touch is one of the senses: we feel heat, cold, pain and pressure with our skin.
fact: «Felt» is the past tense of feel: «She felt tired after the match.»
fact: Feelings tell us about ourselves. If something feels wrong or you feel unsafe, tell a trusted adult.
fact: Useful phrases: feel like (want), feel better, feel sorry for, feel free, feel sick.
exercise: «Feel how soft this is.» What does feel mean here? | To be sad | To hear a sound | *To notice by touch | To think or believe
exercise: «Time feels shorter when you are playing.» What does feels mean here? | To be sick | To touch something | To believe something | *To seem a certain way
exercise: Ella says «I feel that we should help.» What does feel mean here? | To feel sad | To find out by touch | To be sick | *To think or believe
test: «Leaving a group can feel scary, but trusted adults can help.» What does feel mean here? | To touch something | *To seem, or be experienced as, a certain way | To think or believe | To go to sleep
test: «Tiny words like «please» make people feel noticed.» What does feel mean here? | To believe something | To seem cold | To touch something | *To have a feeling inside, so you feel noticed
exam: Which word is a noun meaning the way something feels? | feels | felt | touch | *a feel
